title: 'Expect: 100-continue is forwarded upstream on the chat and JSON routes; a
  node''s 100 Continue can empty the relayed answer'
updated: 2026-10-03T04:15:00Z
---

Found while building the audio routes (k91). _forward_headers passes the client's `Expect` header upstream. curl sends `Expect: 100-continue` with every body above 1 MiB. A node that answers it with `100 Continue` makes Mojo::UserAgent start a fresh response object; the stream relay listens on the first one, so on the audio stream route the client got an empty 200 and the usage event said ok=1. k91 drops the header on the audio routes only.

The chat stream relay and the JSON path build their upstream request from the same forwarded headers and have the same mechanics; nobody tested them. A chat body above 1 MiB (images, long histories) sent by curl is the case.

Wanted:
- reproduce on /v1/chat/completions (stream and non-stream) with a raw fake node that answers 100 Continue; if it fails the same way, drop `expect` in _forward_headers for every route -- Skeid holds the whole body by then, nothing is expected of the node -- and take the special case out of the audio handler
- optional, separate: answer `100 Continue` to the client from _limit_upload once limit and client_auth are fine. Mojolicious sends none, so a curl upload above 1 MiB waits out curl's own one-second timeout before it sends the body.
